    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for 2026-07-10 is anchored by high-ceiling matchups against soft pitching, with **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) leading the charge against Avila. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a high-leverage order spot, making him our premier play of the day. **Dylan Beavers** remains a critical component of our strategy; despite a minor efficiency dip due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s ability to control the run game, his favorable park factor and platoon edge keep him comfortably in the elite scoring tier. Similarly, **Bryce Harper** (68.39) remains a must-start, as his xwOBA upside and a positive park environment allow him to overcome a respectable opponent in Flaherty. **Tyler Freeman** (64.87) is also a strong play, buoyed by a favorable wind forecast and a solid matchup against Ray, providing significant value at the MI slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Daulton Varsho** (53.53), who fell just shy of cracking the starting rotation. While **Daulton Varsho** offers significant SB utility, the optimizer favored **Gavin Sheets** (60.46) due to a superior platoon advantage against Bieber and the heavy SP skill deficit assigned to the opposing pitcher. We are keeping a close watch on **JJ Bleday** (56.85), as his matchup against Imanaga carries a 35% rain risk; should that game be delayed or postponed, **Daulton Varsho** is the next man up to absorb those at-bats. Elsewhere, **Jonathan Aranda** (61.98) earns the UTIL spot over **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.75) primarily due to a superior order position and a favorable platoon profile against Castillo, confirming our commitment to chasing daily efficiency over season-long depth in this 5x5 format.",
